📊 Business Insights & Strategic Recommendations

Amazon Brazil E-Commerce Analytics | MySQL Project

Project Overview

This project analyzes Brazilian e-commerce transactional data to uncover insights into seller performance, customer purchasing behavior, product revenue, payment preferences, delivery efficiency, and customer satisfaction.

Using MySQL, 14 business questions were analyzed to support decision-making across logistics, marketing, finance, merchandising, customer relationship management, and marketplace operations.

The primary objective was to transform transactional data into actionable business intelligence.
Overall Business Interpretation

The results suggest that the marketplace has a geographically concentrated seller network, strong credit card usage, several commercially significant product categories, and opportunities to improve customer engagement and logistics performance.

The findings can support business planning, although some metrics require additional segmentation before operational decisions are made.

2. Seller Performance & Fulfillment Operations
Business Insight

São Paulo dominates seller-side fulfillment activity.

The substantial difference between São Paulo and other states indicates a high concentration of marketplace supply-side operations.

This may reflect a large seller base, higher seller transaction activity, or both.

Strategic Recommendations

Assess warehouse capacity and transportation infrastructure in São Paulo.

Evaluate whether logistics partnerships in Minas Gerais and Paraná could support more balanced regional distribution.

Compare seller locations with customer delivery destinations to identify potential shipping inefficiencies.

Monitor delivery delays and transportation costs across high-volume seller states.

Expected Business Impact: More informed regional fulfillment planning and potential improvements in logistics efficiency.

Q7. Sellers Who Have Never Fulfilled an Order

Key Finding

0 sellers identified.

The follow-up analysis using LEFT JOIN and NOT EXISTS returned no sellers meeting the tested inactivity criteria.

Business Insight

The result suggests that all registered sellers represented in the dataset have fulfilled at least one order, provided the verification included delivered-order status.

This is a positive historical seller-activation finding.

However, historical fulfillment does not necessarily indicate that sellers remain active.

Strategic Recommendations

Track sellers who have not fulfilled orders in the last 30, 60, or 90 days.

Identify sellers with declining order volumes.

Develop re-engagement campaigns for sellers showing signs of inactivity.

Monitor seller retention using recent transaction activity rather than lifetime activity alone.

Expected Business Impact: Improved seller retention monitoring and earlier identification of declining seller participation.

Q11. Sellers Performing Above the Platform Average

Key Finding

The SQL analysis identifies sellers whose recorded order activity exceeds the average across sellers.

The supplied SQL file does not contain the numerical average or the number of qualifying sellers.

Business Insight

Above-average seller performance provides a useful starting point for identifying sellers who contribute more transaction activity than their peers.

However, order volume alone does not establish seller quality.

High-volume sellers may still experience poor delivery performance, cancellations, or negative customer reviews.

Strategic Recommendations

Use above-average delivered-order volume as an initial seller segmentation criterion.

Combine seller order volume with customer review scores and delivery reliability.

Identify consistently high-performing sellers for recognition programs.

Investigate operational practices used by successful sellers.

Expected Business Impact: Better seller segmentation and a more balanced foundation for seller recognition programs.

3. Revenue & Product Performance

Q2. Cumulative Revenue by Product Category

Key Finding

The analysis calculates cumulative product revenue over time using SQL window functions.

The supplied SQL file contains the calculation, but not the numerical output needed to identify specific category growth patterns.

Business Insight

Cumulative revenue provides visibility into how category sales build over time.

This analysis can help distinguish categories with consistent revenue accumulation from those experiencing concentrated periods of demand.

It also creates a foundation for comparing actual revenue performance against business targets.

Strategic Recommendations

Compare cumulative revenue against monthly category targets.

Identify categories that reach sales targets early or late in a reporting period.

Investigate revenue spikes alongside promotional activity.

Use category-level revenue trends to support inventory planning.

Expected Business Impact: Improved revenue monitoring and more informed promotional scheduling

