Q13. Customers Who Have Never Submitted a Review

Key Finding

716 unique customers were identified who placed at least one order but had no recorded reviews across their purchase history.

Business Insight

These 716 customers represent a specific audience for post-purchase engagement campaigns.

Their absence of review activity creates an opportunity to increase customer feedback participation.

However, customers who do not submit reviews are not necessarily dissatisfied.

Strategic Recommendations

Send targeted review reminders after successful delivery.

Prioritize repeat purchasers who have never submitted feedback.

Measure the proportion of purchasing customers who have never reviewed.

Track review participation before and after engagement campaigns.

Avoid excessive reminders that could negatively affect customer experience.

Expected Business Impact: Increased customer feedback participation and improved review coverage.

