7. Demand Forecasting & Seasonality

Q14. Highest-Order-Volume Month
Business Insight

August recorded the highest order count in the month-level aggregation.

May and July also recorded relatively high transaction volumes.

This suggests that these months deserve further investigation for demand planning.

However, the SQL query combines matching calendar months across years. Therefore, the result does not necessarily identify the highest-volume individual month-year period.

Strategic Recommendations

Analyze monthly demand separately by year.

Identify whether high-demand periods recur consistently.

Compare demand spikes with major promotional events.

Use validated seasonal patterns to plan inventory and warehouse staffing.

Monitor category-level demand during high-volume periods.

Expected Business Impact: More informed forecasting and operational capacity planning.

8. Cross-Functional Business Insights

The most valuable opportunities emerge when findings from different business functions are considered together.

Insight 1: São Paulo Is Central to Marketplace Activity

São Paulo leads both seller-side fulfillment activity and customer purchasing activity.

Business Opportunity: Compare supply-side and demand-side geography to determine whether fulfillment infrastructure is appropriately distributed.

Insight 2: Revenue Performance and Customer Satisfaction Should Be Connected

The analysis identifies leading revenue categories and differences in category review scores.

Business Opportunity: Combine revenue and satisfaction metrics to identify categories that are commercially important but may require quality improvements.

Insight 3: Customer Value Can Support Targeted Engagement

The analysis identifies high-spending customers and 716 purchasing customers without recorded reviews.

Business Opportunity: Develop separate engagement strategies for valuable repeat customers and customers who have not participated in review programs.

Insight 4: Delivery Efficiency May Be Related to Regional Satisfaction

The median delivery duration is 10 days, while average review scores vary across states.

Business Opportunity: Investigate whether delivery performance and customer satisfaction are associated at the regional level.

This relationship requires further analysis and should not be assumed from the existing results.

Insight 5: Seller Performance Requires Multiple Metrics

The analysis covers seller activity, historical fulfillment, and above-average seller performance.

Business Opportunity: Develop a seller performance framework combining fulfilled-order volume, delivery reliability, customer satisfaction, and recent activity.
